####################################################################
# PS-11273: the component must not crash when the server aborts.
#
# When the server terminates early - here by way of an invalid
# --authentication-policy - it never calls the component's deinit
# function, so whatever the component left behind at namespace scope is
# torn down during static destruction instead. Destroying AuditLogFilter
# that late destroys its AuditUdf member, and
# AuditUdf::deinit() -> SysVars::get_comp_registry_srv() then touches a
# static that may already be gone. The server died a second time on top
# of the configuration error:
#
#   mysqld got signal 6
#    #11 audit_log_filter::SysVars::get_comp_registry_srv()
#    #12 audit_log_filter::AuditUdf::deinit()
#    #13 audit_log_filter::AuditUdf::~AuditUdf()
#    #15 std::unique_ptr<audit_log_filter::AuditUdf>::~unique_ptr()
#
# The abort is an assert(), hence the debug build requirement below; a
# release build takes the same path but reads the destroyed object
# instead of stopping.
#
# So the test starts the server with a configuration it has to reject,
# and checks that the only thing wrong with that startup is the
# configuration error itself.
####################################################################

--source include/have_component_audit_log.inc
--source include/have_debug.inc
--source ../inc/audit_tables_init.inc
--source ../inc/audit_comp_install.inc

CALL mtr.add_suppression("Option --authentication-policy is set to an invalid value");
# The rejected configuration is the point of the test, so the abort that
# follows it is expected too.  This does not weaken the assertion below:
# that only looks for "mysqld got signal".
CALL mtr.add_suppression("\\[MY-010119\\] \\[Server\\] Aborting");

--echo ### Shutdown
--source include/shutdown_mysqld.inc

--echo ### Start with invalid option
# The policy names a plugin that does not exist, so authentication_policy::init()
# rejects it and the server aborts.  Do not spell the rejected configuration with
# a server variable (this used to pass --mysql_native_password=OFF): a variable
# that a later version removes turns into "unknown variable", which aborts during
# option parsing instead, long before the component is loaded, and never logs the
# message waited for below.
--let $restart_parameters=--authentication-policy=no_such_auth_plugin
--source include/start_mysqld_expecting_crash.inc

--echo ### Waiting for the error message to occur
--let $grep_pattern=authentication-policy is set to an invalid value
--let $grep_file=$MYSQLTEST_VARDIR/log/mysqld.1.err
--source include/wait_for_pattern_in_file.inc

--echo ### Start again
--let $restart_parameters=restart:
--source include/start_mysqld.inc

--echo ### Check that the server only refused to start, and did not crash
# Checked after the restart because assert_grep.inc needs a server to run on.
# The aborted process is long gone by then, so its error log is complete;
# without the fix this finds the signal 6 raised while the component was
# being torn down at exit.
--let $assert_text=Server rejected the configuration without crashing
--let $assert_file=$MYSQLTEST_VARDIR/log/mysqld.1.err
--let $assert_select=mysqld got signal
--let $assert_count=0
--source include/assert_grep.inc

--source ../inc/audit_comp_uninstall.inc
--source ../inc/audit_tables_cleanup.inc
